stand-rocky9-lvm-xfs-bios — the donor inventory CAPTURED by tools/reloca-test.sh (phase capture)
from the rocky9-lvm-xfs-bios fixture (the BIOS/MBR twin of rocky9-lvm-xfs-uefi: Rocky Linux 9.8
by anaconda/kickstart, see tools/fixtures/README.md): dos label, vda1 /boot xfs (bootable), vda2
PV -> VG rl (swap LV, root LV xfs), no ESP, grub2-pc in the MBR, BLS entries, dracut,
NetworkManager keyfile on ens3, SELinux enforcing, lvm.conf with the devices file.
recipient.inv is the stand's synthetic 20 GiB bios VM (as for the debian bios fixture).
expected.plan = plan_compute over the two: rhel/dracut/i386-pc/bls=1, devices file deleted,
autorelabel, every fstab spec and BLS token kept, dos kept with the donor's label-id, the PV
slot elastic, the root LV by block with grow, no grub_pkgs (bios -> bios). The firmware change
of this donor (bios -> uefi: dos -> gpt, esp-new vda3, grub_pkgs=grub2-efi-x64,shim-x64,
efibootmgr) is computed on the fly in tests/cases/plan.sh against the stand's uefi recipient.
Regenerate after a re-capture: plan_compute donor.inv recipient.inv auto > expected.plan
(swap/PV/VG/LV UUIDs are anaconda's and change with every rebuild of the fixture).
